{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/260467-rules-for-creating-ghost-pcs","id":260467,"title":"Rules for creating ghost PCs?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-19T03:10:32-07:00","id":260467,"title":"Rules for creating ghost PCs?","content":"So, apologies if this has come up somewhere before, I could find nothing on this board or on Google.<br /> <br /> I'm gearing up to play in a Mummy game and another player has expressed interest in playing a ghost forever changed by exposure to Tier 3 of my Words of Dead Hunger Utterance. The ST is somewhat amenable to the idea but found he didn't know where to reference rules for the other player to generate such a character.<br /> <br /> Looking through the NWoD core and Mummy we've been unable to find a base chassis or specific character creation template for ghosts that mirrors the &quot;Mummy template&quot; described on p. 64 of MtC, for building a ghost character. Even if the ST ultimately says no to the other playing making this ghost his PC, I'm interested in finding rules that would support chargenning such an altered ghost as an NPC ally or Blessed dead cultist of my Mummy.<br /> <br /> I guess the frustration is that it seems like there are pretty straightforward rules to create PC cultists (straight NWoD mortal chargen) or even Sadikth but we haven't found such rules for ghosts.<br /> <br /> We haven't looked at the Geist splat rules and weren't sure if that was the route we needed to take (i.e. use Geist chargen and then modify the character based on the effects of Words of Dead Hunger to turn the ghost into a &quot;spectral fire demon&quot; servant to my Mummy). Any suggestions of where to look or what resources we need would be much appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T03:31:03-07:00","id":260483,"title":"","content":"There's a Numen called &quot;Lucid Dead&quot; in the GM section of the Mummy rulebook that gives a ghost the same statistics as a mortal. You have all the same attributes, skills, and merits (barring ones not applicable for a ghost), so you build the character just like any regular mortal character and add ghost abilities.<br /> <br /> Toss in &quot;Old Age&quot; as well, and it has a power stat just like any other supernatural creature. If you houserule that it can raise its &quot;Age&quot; trait with experience, it wouldn't even be all that different from playing any other supernatural creature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T09:03:47-07:00","id":261284,"title":"","content":"Thanks, I think we all missed that. Appreciate it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}